From 3587f73e521aa48ef2a285d7b029cf1b7e0e7378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:22:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: dock previews fit what remains, and the dock menu reads
 as one context menu

Window previews: closing a window from its card left the preview at its old
size until the pointer left and came back. The preview now eases straight to
the cards that remain, 180ms, size and place driven by one timeline so every
frame is centred on its icon and SHELF_SURFACE_GAP from the island. With
reduced motion it changes size at once. It holds its size while a closing
window's card goes, so no frame is drawn at the new size early. A pointer
that closed a window and has not moved does not count as leaving, even when
the preview shrinks away from it. Closing the last window closes the preview
as it always leaves.

Dock menu: the title is the app's name as a menu heading, never a window's
title. Window rows show only when the app has two or more windows. The menu
is grouped as the menu contract groups it: windows; New Window and the app's
actions; how it starts; Pin/Unpin, App Details and Quit. There is one rule
between groups that show and none between items. New Window and Unpin are
unchanged.

Open at Login: every app gets a switch backed by luma-background's login
items (interface version 2, luma-background 0.1.0-1.luma.3). That service
answers from the person's and the system's XDG autostart entries and the
Background portal's entries. When an app's login start is its background
agent, this switch is that agent's decision and the separate "Run in the
Background" row is not shown, so there is one control per start. The row
follows LoginItemsChanged while the menu is open, and is hidden when the
service is not there.

Dropping this patch restores the previous preview and menu.
